{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791892551,"nonce":"NW5W5jCIeFWxpWGKOUjhZ/4nfXo=","title":"Infer bare map constructors from writes in nested scopes","message":"A bare new Map() can get its key/value types from a later loop variable or enum pattern binding. Constructor lookahead runs before those bindings exist, leaving an uncompiled haxe.ds.Map.new call. Track unresolved constructors by local symbol, bind their types when the write is lowered in scope, and rebuild the initializer using that type. Cover indexed writes, set calls, final locals, and enum matches in MapInferredInLoop.hx. Root Map typedefs must remain recognizable before their target is registered.","files":null}]}